   "text": "Etched raised $700M in August at a $21B valuation. Jane Street used the hardware, then led the round. There are now talks of a new one at $40B to $50B.\n\nIt designs its own chip and sells it inside complete server racks. \n\nI went in to understand the company. I came out more interested in why it exists at all.\n\nNvidia has roughly 80% of the AI chip market and a 75% gross margin, up from 70% in mid-2023. Margins are supposed to fall as hardware scales. Nvidia\u2019s went up while quarterly revenue grew 7x.\n\nLast quarter it made $72B of gross profit. That is roughly the entire combined annual revenue of OpenAI and Anthropic, earned in three months.\n\nHere is why that number pulls everyone in.\n\nFor ev",
